<title>GERMANY: German SPD says tax talks with coalition postponed.</title>
<headline>German SPD says tax talks with coalition postponed.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's opposition Social Democrats (SPD) said on Friday that a third round of crucial tax reform talks with the coalition government scheduled for Saturday had been postponed.</p>
<p>A source in the office of SPD parliamentary leader Rudolf Scharping, a member of the opposition negotiating team, confirmed that the meeting had been put off but could not say whether a new date had been set.</p>
</text>
